        <mxCell id="RlecWIhCM_28DGbeUyVt-99" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Pipeline Design&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p data-end=&quot;242&quot; data-start=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Each product will be associated with a single notebook, which may generate multiple DLT pipelines within a single workflow. For instance, Epic will primarily use one notebook that iterates through products to create data flows in a single job. This single job may include:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol data-is-last-node=&quot;&quot; data-end=&quot;346&quot; data-start=&quot;244&quot;&gt;&lt;li data-end=&quot;274&quot; data-start=&quot;244&quot;&gt;A pipeline for encounters&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-end=&quot;315&quot; data-start=&quot;275&quot;&gt;A pipeline for patient demographics&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-is-last-node=&quot;&quot; data-end=&quot;346&quot; data-start=&quot;316&quot;&gt;A pipeline for appointments&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-is-last-node=&quot;&quot; data-end=&quot;346&quot; data-start=&quot;316&quot;&gt;.....&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="RlecWIhCM_28DGbeUyVt-1">
